    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_7a607d3a4f6fd9d09b7bce9a1f5992f8a9007042f73615362bfb5cca942b912f",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The source places Eq. (2.8) beside two other power-weighted integral representations of ζ(s): Eqs. (2.9)-(2.10) use equivalent cosh(y) and exp(y)+1 forms, while Eq. (2.11) uses log(y)-Γ′(y)/Γ(y). The comparison varies the kernel and admissible domain without deriving a transformation among these formulas, so it organizes alternative representations rather than establishing their equivalence or interchangeability.",
