    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0026a8ba24110793309eaaeeb087d6d08dd0ee540de92d39b71441d610bc03b7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source gives complementary residue-theorem views around the same integral representation: the first route engineers a rational x,n kernel whose residues manufacture individual alternating Dirichlet-series terms and whose n-dependence can be summed into Eq. (2.6), whereas the later route sketches reading Eq. (2.8)'s hyperbolic kernel as an alternating nonzero pole lattice after the 1/y subtraction removes the origin contribution.",
